# A1-P01 — Waking Wrong. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1158–1219.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/opening_crash_site_hook.tscn. Playable, top-down.
# Kaelen acts because he thinks other passengers might be alive. There is no
# plane, no wreckage and no bodies; the absence is the mystery.
# Each inspect point runs its own node, in any order. "fused_metal" gives the
# route east, which is what lets the player leave.

~ start
Kaelen: Ow.
Kaelen (Internal): Okay. Breathing. Breathing's step one.
Kaelen: The flight. Where's—
Kaelen: Where's the plane?
do objective Find the plane. Look for survivors.

# The first time the player walks toward the crater's centre.
~ call_out
Kaelen: Hello?
Kaelen: Flight 707! Can anyone hear me?
Kaelen: Anyone?
Kaelen (Internal): Nothing. Not even an alarm.

~ scorched_ground
Kaelen: No fuel smell.
Kaelen (Internal): Everything should smell like fuel. Why doesn't it smell like fuel?

~ fused_metal
Kaelen: That's off the plane. That's...
Kaelen: I think that's off the plane.
do translation_flicker
System: SYSTEM TRACE: RECOVERY SECTOR 04-A.
System: SYSTEM TRACE: LOCAL SETTLEMENT ROUTE — EAST.
do runes_return
Kaelen: No. No, no, I saw that. That was text.
Kaelen (Internal): Okay. Either I hit my head harder than I think, or something just gave me directions.
Kaelen (Internal): East, then. If anyone else walked out of here, they went east.
set ch1_crash_trace_seen
do objective Find people. A settlement east may know what happened to Flight 707.

~ safety_card
Kaelen: Safety card. "In the unlikely event of—"
Kaelen: That's all that's left. Just the number.
Kaelen (Internal): 707. Okay. So it happened. It was real.
set ch1_flight_fragment_found

~ seat_marks
Kaelen: That's a row of seats. That's the shape of a whole row of seats.
Kaelen: So where are the—
Kaelen: No. There were people here. There were people sitting right here.

~ sky
Kaelen: The clouds are going two different ways.
Kaelen: Sure. Great. The sky's broken too.

~ perimeter
Kaelen: Bags. Shoes. Anything.
Kaelen: Come on...

# The player reaches the east road after finding the trace.
~ leave
do sfx distant_cry
Kaelen (Internal): Whatever that was, it isn't a survivor.
Kaelen (Internal): East.

# The player tries to leave before finding the trace.
~ leave_blocked
Kaelen (Internal): I'm not walking off until I know which way they'd have gone.
